      "message": "fix(app): probe reads its picks in the setup frame in a turned setup\n\nThe Probe op seeded its touch from the picked feature with the model's\nown placement (`model::transform_of`), while generation judges the\nstylus against the facets of the setup frame. In a setup that holds the\npart turned, the two reads disagreed: the posted cycle sought a surface\n10 mm inside the part, and nothing refused it.\n\nRead the placement through `setup_align::pose_in`, and carry the setup\nname through `probe_seed`, `probe_from_picks` and `probe_account` - the\nshape #2276 gave the Slot helpers. Add Probe to the verified aligned\nmill kinds, so it generates on `Mill` and `MillTurn`, and name it in the\nrefusal message. Probe is not a turning kind: `verified_turn` and the\nlathe-post refusal stay as they are.\n\nThe proof is `crates/app/tests/setup_align_probe_kinds.rs`: a box turned\nabout two axes seeds the touch on the part as the setup holds it, and\ncuts the same path and posts the same program as a part with that turn\nbaked into its mesh; the part as modelled seeds another touch and cuts\nanother path. A second test pins the safety law: a target written in the\nmodel frame in a turned setup feeds the stylus through the part, and the\nprotected-move law convicts it with a post-blocking warning.\n\nFive sentinels that pinned Probe as refused now name kinds that stay\nunverified: a hand-carried WireContour params read through\n`generation_problem` (in the 2D-kinds, multi-axis and op-frame suites),\na tilted Contour (the tilted-plane branch in `setup_align`), and the\nmill-turn loop. The mill-turn suite now asserts Probe is admitted there.\n\nFixes #2285",
